# Appwrite MCP Server for Zed

Use Appwrite's hosted MCP server from Zed to manage projects and resources with the Agent Panel. Authentication uses Appwrite's browser-based OAuth flow, so no API keys or manually entered secrets are required.

![Appwrite MCP successfully running in Zed](docs/appwrite-mcp-working.png)

## Installation

This extension is not published in the Zed extension gallery. Zed connects to remote MCP servers natively, so the recommended setup needs no extension at all.

### Add the remote server (recommended)

1. Open **Settings > AI > MCP Servers**, select **Add Server**, then **Add Remote Server**.
2. Use this configuration:

   ```json
   {
     "appwrite": {
       "url": "https://mcp.appwrite.io/"
     }
   }
   ```

3. Complete the Appwrite authentication flow in your browser.

The same entry can be added under `context_servers` in your settings file (`zed: open settings file`).

### Install this extension as a dev extension

The extension wraps the same server with [`mcp-remote`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/mcp-remote). To use it, [install Rust with rustup](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install), clone this repository, run `zed: install dev extension` from the Command Palette, and select the cloned folder. Then enable **Appwrite MCP Server** in **Settings > AI > MCP Servers** and complete the authentication flow in your browser.

## Enable Appwrite tools

Open the Agent Panel, select the active agent profile, and enable the Appwrite MCP tools for that profile. You can then test the connection with:

> Use Appwrite to show my workspace context and list my projects.

Zed asks for confirmation before tool calls by default. Review and approve write operations before they run.

![Appwrite MCP successfully completing a write operation in Zed](docs/appwrite-mcp-write.png)

## Troubleshooting

### The browser did not open

Restart the Appwrite server from **Settings > AI > MCP Servers**. If the browser still does not open, copy the authentication URL from the server output and open it manually.

### The server status is not green

Open **Settings > AI > MCP Servers** and check the indicator next to the Appwrite server. Restart the server. With the dev extension, also confirm that Zed was able to install the `mcp-remote` npm package.

### The OAuth session needs to be refreshed

Sign out or clear the saved Appwrite MCP authorization from the server controls, restart the server, and complete the browser authentication flow again.

### Inspect logs

Run `zed: open log` from the Command Palette and search for `appwrite` or `mcp-remote`.

